From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] A bound listbox is the control's own wherever the widget mounted it

optionsOf, the ONLY place in this runner that enumerates an option list for
reporting, was narrower than the chooser in the same file in three ways, and
each one turns a menu that is fully present in the DOM into "this employer
offers no choices" - which downstream is a required question that can never be
answered, because the product must send one of the control's own exact option
strings and it has none to send.

Measured on mehekmandal05@gmail.com 2026-09-03: of 179 unanswered REQUIRED
choice questions across the packet queue, 160 carry a completely EMPTY option
list, and 19 packets are blocked on nothing else.

  1. SIBLING-ONLY. listbox.parentElement === el.parentElement meant a menu
     portalled to <body> was never this opener's - which is where downshift,
     React Select with menuPortalTarget, Radix, MUI and Headless UI all put it.
     This is the exact defect measured on cbsconsulting.recruitee.com 2026-08-28
     and already fixed for the CHOOSER (readOpenerPortalListbox, and the three
     assertions in test/recruitee-listbox-portal-scope-dom.test.js). So the two
     layers disagreed about which listbox is a control's own: the chooser could
     commit an option the reader was unable to report.
  2. aria-owns WAS NEVER READ, though it is the ARIA 1.0 spelling of the same
     forward statement and Select2 and jQuery UI still write it. The chooser
     reads aria-controls then aria-owns; this read only the first.
  3. THE REFERENCE HAD TO LAND ON THE LISTBOX ITSELF, so the common spelling
     where aria-controls names the popup CONTAINER and the list sits one node
     inside it was refused outright.

Plus the row vocabulary: only [role="option"] counted, so a <ul role="listbox">
whose rows are plain <li> - Select2's results list, every hand-rolled downshift
menu - read as zero rows off a menu that was entirely present.

The discipline that bounds this is unchanged and does all the work: exactly ONE
bound candidate or nothing is inferred, and a candidate must hold at least one
option row, so an empty popup shell can become neither a vocabulary nor an
ambiguity.

VERIFIED against seven stub DOMs (stratus-patches/verify-bound-listbox.mjs in
the volley-backend branch fix/choice-options-never-captured). Five return an
empty list before this patch and the correct list after; the two safety shapes -
two listboxes naming one opener, and a portal listbox that does not name the
opener - are refused identically before and after.

NOTE ON PROVENANCE: produced by an agent that had no git access to this repo, so
it is delivered as a patch rather than as a commit. Apply with:
  git checkout -b fix/choice-options-never-captured origin/main
  git am < 0001-bound-listbox-wherever-mounted.patch
Then run: npm test (test/question-label-dom.test.js covers optionsOf directly)
and npm run test:choice-parity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
